invariant: INV-13
file: tls_write.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_fail takes close_notify as an error alert, so a caller that
  passes 0 fails the session and sends a close_notify it did not mean.
  RFC 9846 §6.1 makes it a closure alert, which ch_close sends.
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires CH_EINVAL and no send for it.

--- old
static const uint8_t error_alerts[] = {
    10,  // unexpected_message
--- new
static const uint8_t error_alerts[] = {
    0,   // close_notify
    10,  // unexpected_message
